   "evidence": "`grep -c toExclKinematics` over `EpsilonEridani/` \u2192 26 hits, all in this new file; lines 202\u2013299 (`MX2_eq_\u2026` through `MX2_congr`) use `deltaTarget`/`pX` directly and never the bridge. `ExclKinematics` (Exclusive/Kinematics/Basic.lean:32\u201352) has fields `phiL phiH : \u211d` with no defining relation, and documents `qPrime` as \"the produced real photon (DVCS) or meson (DVMP)\", not a mass-selected system.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Kinematics/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `toExclKinematics` and the eleven lemmas, and state the sign-independence of `t` directly: `lemma tMom_eq_pPrime_sub_p_sq (g) (K) : tMom g K = g (K.pPrime - K.p) (K.pPrime - K.p)`, proved from `deltaTarget` and `neg_sub` with `map_neg`. If the exclusive layer really is to be reused (roadmap: diffraction \"reuses rather than re-derives\" the exclusive `t`), then make the diffractive invariants go through the bridge instead of defining them in parallel and reconciling afterwards \u2014 not both.",
   "issue": "`toExclKinematics` plus its eleven companion lemmas (`toExclKinematics_p` \u2026 `toExclKinematics_phiH`, `delta_toExclKinematics`, `tMom_toExclKinematics`, `Q2_toExclKinematics`, lines 147\u2013200) are used nowhere \u2014 grep for `toExclKinematics` yields hits only inside this file, all within the bridge block. The only fact they deliver is that `t` is sign-convention independent, and the bridge requires inventing `phiL phiH : \u211d`, which the `ExclKinematics` record constrains by nothing, so they never specialize to any diffractive datum. Roadmap \u00a70.1 asks for the variables and the four identities, not an embedding into the exclusive record.",
   "line": "147"
  }
